{"duration_api_ms":163299,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"88ec99ea-58c2-4bbe-bcd0-7a536889a356","total_cost_usd":0.4791256,"usage":{"input_tokens":22,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19007,"cache_read_input_tokens":285313,"output_tokens":16347,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":8333},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19007},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":22,"outputTokens":16347,"cacheReadInputTokens":285313,"cacheCreationInputTokens":19007,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4791256,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":8333,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":11,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written the answer to `/work/answer.md` and marked it `[opus] FINAL` on the board. Argon never posted, so no one else has reviewed it.\n\n**Condition (all values positive):** the Vickrey-nearest point equals the centroid of F exactly when one of these holds:\n1. v_P ≤ min(v_A, v_B, v_C). VCG then charges everyone 0, and F is the triangle {p ≥ 0, Σp = v_P}.\n2. v_P ≥ v_i + v_j for every pair of winners. F is again a triangle.\n3. v_A = v_B = v_C.\n\nIn every other case the two points differ, even when no value cap binds at the Vickrey-nearest point. So the two-winner \"midpoint\" result does not carry over to three winners.\n\n**Proof idea:**\n- **Reduction:** written in terms of each winner's surplus, F becomes a box cut by a plane. The Vickrey-nearest point is then a projection onto that slice, computed by water-filling.\n- **When it holds:** under condition 1 or 2, F is a triangle and both points are its center. Under condition 3, everything is symmetric, so both points sit at the same symmetric point.\n- **When it fails:** a swap-symmetry argument shows the centroid sits strictly higher in the coordinate with the larger cap than in the smallest-cap one. Water-filling either gives those two coordinates the same value, or pushes the smallest-cap coordinate to its cap, where the centroid can't be. Either way the points differ.\n\n**Example where they differ:** v_P = 4, (v_A, v_B, v_C) = (2, 3, 4). F is a pentagon. The Vickrey-nearest point is (4/3, 4/3, 4/3) and the centroid is (31/33, 46/33, 5/3). The file also has worked examples where they agree, one for each condition.\n\n**Checks:**\n- **Reduced form:** a scan of 20,000 random instances agreed with the condition. The only mismatch I printed was a rounding artifact just past the boundary of condition 1.\n- **Original constraints:** 3,000 random integer instances agreed except 4. Those 4 are reorderings of v = (3, 6, 9), v_P = 15, where the optimizer stopped at the wrong point. Computing that case by hand shows the two points are equal there, as the condition predicts.\n\nThe check scripts are `opus_scan.py` and `opus_check2.py` in `/work`.","ttft_ms":2115,"type":"result","duration_ms":359779,"uuid":"10b6df98-89ca-4f27-ac5d-34b9fe53d474","ttft_stream_ms":1726,"time_to_request_ms":56,"first_content_frame_ms":1726,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
